WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.501 --> 00:00:03.035
-We'll be right back with
a performance from Dayglow.

00:00:03.035 --> 00:00:04.136
Stick around!

00:00:04.136 --> 00:00:05.138
[ Cheers and applause ]
He's amazing.

00:00:05.138 --> 00:00:07.039
♪♪

00:00:07.039 --> 00:00:10.110
How is your vinyl collection?
-It's good. It's good.

00:00:10.110 --> 00:00:12.945
-Is it anywhere near Questlove's
vinyl collection?

00:00:12.945 --> 00:00:17.683
-Here's the thing.
I feel like I have a collection.

00:00:17.683 --> 00:00:20.052
Questlove has a problem.
-Yeah, really.

00:00:20.052 --> 00:00:21.420
-He's a hoarder.
-Yeah.

00:00:21.420 --> 00:00:24.523
-Yeah. I have a
healthy collection of records.

00:00:24.523 --> 00:00:26.759
I think Questlove is a hoarder.

00:00:26.759 --> 00:00:29.228
I think what we have right now
is an opportunity

00:00:29.228 --> 00:00:30.997
to have an intervention,

00:00:30.997 --> 00:00:34.234
where we all just take
some records away from him.

00:00:34.234 --> 00:00:35.234
-Yes.

00:00:35.234 --> 00:00:36.235
-Yeah.
-No.

00:00:36.235 --> 00:00:37.503
-Yeah.
-Yeah.

00:00:37.503 --> 00:00:40.205
This actually isn't even an
audience, Questlove.

00:00:40.205 --> 00:00:44.577
-No. These are all just
music friends who were like,

00:00:44.577 --> 00:00:46.779
"We each need to take
like 100 records

00:00:46.779 --> 00:00:48.114
out of your collection

00:00:48.114 --> 00:00:49.115
just to get you back to
a healthy place."

00:00:49.115 --> 00:00:51.851
-Just 100?
-Yeah, just 100 each.

00:00:51.851 --> 00:00:52.886
-Okay, cool.
-Yeah.

00:00:52.886 --> 00:00:55.154
-Do you get flashbacks still

00:00:55.154 --> 00:00:56.256
when you come into
this building?

00:00:56.256 --> 00:00:57.390
-Yeah. Oh, yeah.

00:00:57.390 --> 00:00:59.491
No, I mean, I've been
in this building

00:00:59.491 --> 00:01:00.693
since I was 19 years old.

00:01:00.693 --> 00:01:02.161
-Yeah, I've known you for,

00:01:02.161 --> 00:01:04.497
gosh, probably
has to be 20 years.

00:01:04.497 --> 00:01:06.098
-Yeah, well, I mean, I'm 78.

00:01:06.098 --> 00:01:07.366
-Oh, my gosh!
You look fantastic.

00:01:07.366 --> 00:01:09.736
-Thank you very much. Yeah.
-Wow. That's great.

00:01:09.736 --> 00:01:12.638
-I was moisturizing a lot
this pandemic.

00:01:12.638 --> 00:01:17.043
-You auditioned to be
a writer on "SNL," right?

00:01:17.043 --> 00:01:18.911
-I did, yeah. I interviewed.

00:01:18.911 --> 00:01:19.946
I actually interviewed
with Tina.

00:01:19.946 --> 00:01:21.380
-Wow!

00:01:21.380 --> 00:01:24.517
-And I had probably

00:01:24.517 --> 00:01:26.118
the worst interview a
person could have.

00:01:26.118 --> 00:01:27.486
'Cause here's the thing.

00:01:27.486 --> 00:01:30.056
When I got the job --
When I interviewed for the job,

00:01:30.056 --> 00:01:31.124
I didn't have an agent.

00:01:31.124 --> 00:01:34.660
It was just through their --

00:01:34.660 --> 00:01:36.695
'cause I had interned here
when I was 19.

00:01:36.695 --> 00:01:40.066
And then Mike Shoemaker
and Colin Quinn

00:01:40.066 --> 00:01:42.868
had suggested me as a writer

00:01:42.868 --> 00:01:45.604
because Colin had read
some of my sketches and stuff.

00:01:45.604 --> 00:01:49.041
And, so, I came in, and because
I didn't have an agent,

00:01:49.041 --> 00:01:50.242
I didn't know what to do

00:01:50.242 --> 00:01:51.877
and I didn't know
what to expect.

00:01:51.877 --> 00:01:54.280
And, so, the only person
I could talk to was

00:01:54.280 --> 00:01:56.783
my stepfather,
who just works in, like,

00:01:56.783 --> 00:02:00.119
the accounting department
for an airline in Texas.

00:02:00.119 --> 00:02:01.453
And he was like,
"Well, you know,

00:02:01.453 --> 00:02:03.055
it's a job interview,

00:02:03.055 --> 00:02:04.824
so you need to treat it
like a job interview.

00:02:04.824 --> 00:02:07.694
But it's not a real job,
because it's TV,

00:02:07.694 --> 00:02:10.363
so you don't need
to wear, like, a suit,

00:02:10.363 --> 00:02:13.232
but maybe wear, like,
khaki slacks and a blazer

00:02:13.232 --> 00:02:15.401
and carry a little briefcase."

00:02:15.401 --> 00:02:18.304
And that's what I did.
-What?!

00:02:18.304 --> 00:02:19.372
-You came in with a briefcase?

00:02:19.372 --> 00:02:20.573
-I came in with
a little briefcase.

00:02:20.573 --> 00:02:22.307
-What was in the briefcase?

00:02:22.307 --> 00:02:24.544
-Just my plane ticket.

00:02:24.544 --> 00:02:29.181
My plane ticket and probably
a "Highlights" magazine.

00:02:29.181 --> 00:02:31.784
But I came in and I looked like

00:02:31.784 --> 00:02:33.453
I was coming in for a bank loan.

00:02:33.453 --> 00:02:36.155
And I remember
I sat across from Tina

00:02:36.155 --> 00:02:37.657
and a bunch of
the other writers.

00:02:37.657 --> 00:02:39.258
And they're all having fun,

00:02:39.258 --> 00:02:41.193
and Tina is
just trying to, like,

00:02:41.193 --> 00:02:42.895
get me to show my personality.

00:02:42.895 --> 00:02:45.531
And I'm just answering
everything like, "Uh-huh.

00:02:45.531 --> 00:02:46.932
Yes.

00:02:46.932 --> 00:02:49.168
No, ma'am. Yes, ma'am.

00:02:49.168 --> 00:02:50.303
Sure, ma'am."

00:02:50.303 --> 00:02:52.105
-Oh, my gosh.
-"That's the door, ma'am?

00:02:52.105 --> 00:02:53.472
Okay."
-"Okay. Bye, ma'am."

00:02:53.472 --> 00:02:55.074
-"Bye, ma'am."

00:02:55.074 --> 00:02:56.809
-"See you never."
-Yeah.

00:02:56.809 --> 00:02:58.511
Well, and then, because I didn't
have an agent, like,

00:02:58.511 --> 00:03:00.213
normally,
if you have an agent, like,

00:03:00.213 --> 00:03:03.315
your agent follows up for you
and they do all that stuff.

00:03:03.315 --> 00:03:04.683
I didn't have that.

00:03:04.683 --> 00:03:07.954
The only person I knew who
I could contact at the show

00:03:07.954 --> 00:03:10.356
was one of Lorne's assistants.

00:03:10.356 --> 00:03:13.192
And so I was just calling
Lorne's assistant like,

00:03:13.192 --> 00:03:15.761
"Hey, have you heard
anything about the show?"

00:03:15.761 --> 00:03:18.597
And, like, Lorne's assistant --
like, to me,

00:03:18.597 --> 00:03:20.967
that was the most powerful
person I knew at the show,

00:03:20.967 --> 00:03:22.668
but, like, an assistant isn't

00:03:22.668 --> 00:03:24.771
the most powerful person
at a show.

00:03:24.771 --> 00:03:26.372
And he -- poor guy --
was just like,

00:03:26.372 --> 00:03:28.308
"Yeah, man, I think you're
still in the mix.

00:03:28.308 --> 00:03:30.310
Like, I'll put in
a good word for you."

